spoiler alert

All right, I'm peeved...  My Valkyrie was all set to go for the amulet.
I find the vibrating square, then check my inventory, and discover that
the candelabrum is cursed.  Using my handy-dandy orb of fate, I pop up to
an altar, whip up some holy water, and uncurse it, in the process dusting
the wizard and his buddies once or twice, and sacrificing any stray corpses
I see.

At one point, I dropped everything on the altar and picked it all up again
to amke known all the cursed/uncursed status, but all seemed well.  I pop
back down to the vibrating square, light the candle, ring the bell, and
discover that the book is gone!  All right, I figure, the wiz must have
stolen it without my noticing, so I go back to all the places I killed
him, cleaning out the levels in search of the amulet.  No luck.  I'm
getting worried that it was lost to a bug.  I checked the sources, but
I can't find anything to indicate that there might be some way for the
book to teleport somewhere.  Other people have reported the same problems,
so it can't be just me...

Does anyone have a utility to list the contents of a save file, so I can
see if the book is still there?  (I'm running on an IBM PC, but I can compile
something if needed.)

